  <revision rev="5" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>00339a1bf6b5a5ffa41ff7732750914f</srcmd5>
    <version>1.2.11</version>
    <time>1786543934</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 1.2.11

Small additive upstream release: a new TracePolicy dataclass and omit_payload
helper in langgraph.types (both added to __all__), a trace_policy argument on
StateGraph.add_node, and stale noqa cleanup. No API removals and no change to
execution behaviour.

No dependency floors changed -- the dependency block is byte-identical to
1.2.10, and the langchain-core floor stays &gt;= 1.4.7 with a &lt; 2 ceiling, so
this is unaffected by the langchain-core 1.5.4 update submitted separately.

Verified on aarch64: build green, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings. The %check
remains byte-compilation only, because upstream's tests/conftest.py
unconditionally imports Postgres and SQLite checkpoint backends that are not
packaged.</comment>
    <requestid>1370778</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="6" vrev="2">
    <srcmd5>d397ad604d7cedce4b88dfd181787edd</srcmd5>
    <version>1.2.11</version>
    <time>1787063838</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Reproducibility fix by bmwiedemann (sr#1371636, accepted into devel): move the
hash-based bytecode recompilation and fdupes from %check to %install so the
package no longer varies when built with --nocheck (boo#1227364), plus a
follow-up comment cleanup.</comment>
    <requestid>1371641</requestid>
  </revision>
